Fix supplied function. Import Empty from queue. poll catches ONLY Empty around get_nowait, schedules next poll and RETURNS there. On successful dequeue call callback OUTSIDE except and never reschedule. Save root.after return value in after_id list [None]; cancel calls root.after_cancel(after_id[0]) if not None (never pass function). cancel marks cancelled[0]=True. Initial call root.after(0,poll) storing id, not poll(). On entry poll sets after_id[0]=None. catch tk.TclError only around after/after_cancel. Keep thread daemon, worker only queue operations. Return corrected source only, no prose.
FILE tasks/background_job/background_job.py
import threading
from queue import Queue
import tkinter as tk

def start_job(root, work, on_success, on_error):
    q = Queue()
    cancelled = [False]
    
    def worker():
        try:
            result = work()
            q.put((True, result))
        except Exception as e:
            q.put((False, e))
    
    t = threading.Thread(target=worker, daemon=True)
    t.start()
    
    def poll():
        if cancelled[0]: return
        try:
            success, data = q.get_nowait()
            if success: on_success(data)
            else: on_error(data)
        except Exception: pass
        
        try:
            root.after(50, poll)
        except tk.TclError:
            pass
    
    def cancel():
        cancelled[0] = True
        try: root.after_cancel(poll) if hasattr(root.after, 'cancel') else None
        except tk.TclError: pass
    
    poll()
    return cancel
